<head>
	<title></title>
</head>
<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Thank you for notifying Qantas of your mobility aid.<br />
<br />
Your mobility aid details have been added to your booking &lt;INSERT PNR&gt;<br />
<br />
If your mobility aid is battery powered, Qantas Dangerous Goods approval must be obtained for the battery prior to uplift.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
If your mobility aid needs to be adjusted or broken down, you are responsible for assembling and disassembling your Mobility Aid where you are able to do so. Where assistance is required, Airport Ground staff will ask you to explain, instruct and supervise the assembling, or disassembling of your Mobility Aid(s). This may include disconnection and connection of the battery.<br />
<br />
<strong>For Domestic and Regional departures</strong><br />
<br />
Passengers who require mobility aid assistance are required to be at the airport:
<ul>
	<li>60 minutes before departure at domestic terminals</li>
</ul>
At least 3 hours before departure at international terminals (applicable to domestic services of an international flight)<br />
<br />
Passengers with specific needs will generally board before and disembark after other passengers.<br />
<br />
If you choose to surrender your mobility aid at the departure gate, you must check-in, have completed security formalities and be at the departure gate:
<ul>
	<li>40 minutes before departure at domestic terminals</li>
	<li>60 minutes before departure at international terminals (applicable to domestic services of an international flight)</li>
</ul>
<br />
If you are travelling on a Qantaslink flight, please be aware that there are no aisle chairs available inflight, so access to the lavatory may not be possible.<br />
<br />
For more information please refer to the following link:<a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/travelling-with-specific-needs/accessible-toilets-onboard.html"> https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/travelling-with-specific-needs/accessible-toilets-onboard.html</a><br />
<br />
<strong>For International departures</strong><br />
<br />
Passengers who require mobility aid assistance are required to be at the airport:
<ul>
	<li>At least 3 hours before departure at international terminals</li>
</ul>
Passengers with specific needs will generally board before and disembark after other passengers. If you choose to surrender your mobility aid at the departure gate, you must check-in, have completed security and immigration formalities and be at the departure gate:

<ul>
	<li>60 minutes before departure at international terminals</li>
</ul>
If you’ve purchased a ticket that includes travel on another airline, be aware not all airlines offer the same specific assistance as Qantas. If travelling on another airline, you’ll need to discuss your specific assistance requirements both with the other airline and with Qantas.<br />
<br />
If you require further assistance with your mobility aid, please reply back to this email or contact the Qantas Customer Specific Needs team between 6am and 10pm (AEST), Monday to Sunday on 1800 177 474 (within Australia) or +61 2 9123 7471 (outside Australia) on 1800 177 474, option 3</body>
</html>